Mr. Pen Sovicheat said:
Mr. Sovichet said that the Ministry of Commerce had further instructed Green Trade, a company controlled by the Ministry of Commerce, to act quickly and in a timely manner to address the plight of people who are implementing blockade measures. In the red area in the three districts of Phnom Penh.
The ministry is also preparing to add some essential commodities to meet the needs of the people during this difficult time, such as dried fish, fried fish, beets and other strategic foods that can be stored for a long time.
On April 15, 2021, the Ministry of Commerce started selling mobile rice and noodles in Phnom Penh at a lower price than the market to help people by buying a bag of rice and a box of noodles.
For 5 days from April 15-19, 2021, the Ministry of Commerce's mobile vehicles sold a total of 297 boxes of rice, 1,975 boxes of fish sauce, a total of 136 bags of soy sauce to people in the closed area of Phnom Penh and Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
