Wing has been licensed by the National Bank of Cambodia to operate as a commercial bank through its extensive digital financial system.
Wing Cambodia Limited, a leading mobile financial services provider in Cambodia, has received a commercial banking license from the National Bank of Cambodia.
This license allows Wing to operate as a commercial bank under the name of Wing Cambodia MK.
Oknha Kith Meng, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Wing Bank, said:
With innovative technology and extensive knowledge of the local market, Wing Bank, our Wing agents and our partners are working together to bridge the gap by providing financial instruments to people outside the banking network.
With this license, Wing Bank can provide a wide range of banking products and services to all Cambodians, such as lending and receiving deposits from the public.
These services will complement Wing's existing digital financial services and are offered through an extensive network of more than 9,300 Wing agents and Wing smartphone applications.
Wing will continue to run its business as usual without affecting the existing services provided through Wing agents and the Wing smartphone app.
We will continue to work closely with partners and the public to promote the financial environment in Cambodia.
The license, obtained from the National Bank of Cambodia, will strengthen Wing's vision of improving the daily lives of people outside the banking network.
Since its inception in 2009, Wing has strived to empower Cambodians by providing them with access to reliable, secure and secure financial services.
