Low risk trading pairs and high weekly profit opportunities
The USDCAD and the Canadian dollar have been fluctuating and may continue to fall in the coming weeks as the Canadian dollar strengthens.
This trend is due to the bilateral relationship on oil production and economies of the two countries, with Canada being one of the major US oil suppliers resuming its economic activities, leading to greater demand for oil. .
Excessive oil exports to the United States today have strengthened the value of the Canadian dollar, making it easier for investors to analyze destinations and seize lucrative trading opportunities.
Since 1994, Canada and the United States have had an understanding and concession agreement on import and export tariffs, known as the North American Free Trade Agreement (NAFTA).
The new US President Joe Biden has also stated his intention to maintain good relations with the United States during his term in office.
The two countries, meanwhile, have similar interest rate policies and currently have similar interest rates near zero.
These factors have played an important role in keeping the USDCAD gap unchanged with low trading risk.
