Why the stock market can bring financial freedom when retiring
Financial freedom is the main desire that everyone expects.
Setting clear life goals and developing a detailed financial plan is believed to be the path to financial success.
What is financial freedom?
Financial freedom is divided into two types: financial freedom now and financial freedom in the future, that is, when retirement, almost all income is lost while in the age of not being able to do business.
This second situation has generally become a serious challenge in Cambodia because most people do not pay much attention to it.
How to get financial freedom when you retire?
Set financial goals When you retire, you should set clear financial goals.
For example, what kind of life do you want to live when you retire, how much money do you have to have then, at what age will you retire to know how much time you have left now to plan.
Setting clear and appropriate goals leads to more realistic goals.
Managing Income, Expenditure and Savings To achieve your goals, you need to plan your budget, starting with managing your income and expenses.
Reduce unnecessary expenses and make sure the cost is lower than your income so that you can save some money to achieve your goals and aspirations.
Reducing expenses alone is not enough, you should maximize your income as much as possible, such as by finding extra part-time work, starting your own business, saving money to invest in financial instruments.
Investing The key to financial freedom is to invest your savings in expanding your sources of income as much as possible, based on the principle of making money.
Popular investments in Cambodia today include business ventures with partners, real estate investments, long-term bank savings, and investments in financial instruments such as stocks.
Each investment offers different rates of return and risk and is suitable for different investment goals.
Why Stocks Are the Best Choice to Invest for Financial Freedom in Retirement?
A passive source of income, as opposed to working and running your own business, you can only earn money if you go out and do it. Earn money without having to go to work.
Having a good company that is transparent and strong already earns you money is a smart passive income generator.
There are two types of income from stock investment: income from dividend distribution and capital gains.
You will receive a dividend based on the profit the company earns and the percentage of shares you hold.
As for your capital gain, you will get it when the market share price rises.
Low capital required and easy to get started on the Cambodia Securities Exchange You can order one or more shares at the current minimum price below R2,000.
So you can afford to save money to invest without much capital, such as real estate investment and other investments.
High-income sustainability Investing in stocks not only makes it easier for investors to earn extra income, but also provides a sustainable source of income.
This means that as long as the company continues to operate in a profitable and profitable business, you remain part of the company and receive a permanent dividend dividend for the children.
High growth potential Investment in stocks listed on the stock exchange can have high growth potential in the long run because the listed stocks are all potential and reliable companies. Pass the correct assessment and meet all standard requirements such as accounting records, corporate governance, capital, profit and so on.
You know that a business can grow and make unlimited profits, so if you invest in stocks of companies with high long-term potential and high growth, you will be able to earn a lot of capital in the future.
Stocks are now the best choice for long-term investment with the goal of gaining financial freedom when you retire, as they can provide a passive income on a regular basis from now to future offspring, in addition to operating income. Occupation and personal business.
And if you know how to analyze and choose the right company with high growth like Facebook, for example, saving little by little from now until you retire, you can become a millionaire.
