Official of the General Department of Taxation confirms the type of non-taxable assets, capital gains
This was revealed at a seminar on capital gains tax on 22 February in Phnom Penh.
This is according to the press release of the General Department of Taxation.
Mr. Ken Sambath, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Taxation, stated that the tax on capital gains is exempt from the sale and transfer of some capital, such as property belonging to state institutions, property belonging to foreign consular missions, international organizations, technical cooperation agencies of Other governments.
The Royal Government also decided to waive the tax on capital gains for the sale and transfer of agricultural land owned or occupied by people who are farmers who are actually growing crops and have a residence in the commune on the land that is farming.
According to Mr. Sambath.
The Royal Government has decided to postpone the implementation of the capital gains tax, which was originally intended to be implemented in 2021 until the beginning of 2022, due to the 19-Kovid epidemic, which is having a negative impact on the real estate sector in Cambodia after some associations proposed Please delay the implementation.
Capital gains tax shall apply to the sale or transfer of property or to establish the right to control property or to register for the transfer of ownership or possession rights.
According to the proclamation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance dated April 1, 2020, this tax is paid from the sale of some real estate such as land, buildings, shares, licenses, patents, bonds and currency, which is subject to 20% tax.
Mr. Sambath said that the application of capital gains tax was also favored to the original residence of the taxpayer who held it for at least five years before the sale and transfer.
In case there is more than one residence or the taxpayer and the spouse have different residences, only one residence is allowed as the original residence.
At the same time, the property in the circle of relatives as stated in the provisions on stamp duty, except for the transfer of ownership or possession of the property between siblings and siblings between parents-in-law and son-in-law and between grandparents, in-laws and the property to be Sold or transferred for public benefit in accordance with the Immigration Act.
Mr. Sambath said that the implementation of the tax on capital gains would ensure the equity of taxation of legal entities, and would also ensure fair competition.
He said that the implementation of the capital gains tax will also contribute to stabilizing property prices by reducing the inflated real estate prices that people and investors can buy real estate at affordable prices.
According to the press release, residents who have already registered for tax and declared annual income tax will no longer be subject to this tax.
This capital gains tax is levied only on capital gains achieved at the time of the sale or transfer of capital, in the case of non-profits there is no tax obligation.
