So, I decided to do politics, I will not leave anywhere other than my hometown.
Although Kranh did not leave the country, he expressed safety concerns in his daily life, as the political situation did not provide favorable conditions for the opposition.
When asked if he had ever been dragged or threatened, Kang Kimhak declined to comment.
Mr. Kang Kimhak left his hometown to enter politics in 1998 through former Sam Rainsy Party lawmaker Cheam Channy as his assistant and has been campaigning with Mr. Cheam Channy ever since.
With high ambitions to become a top politician like a Member of Parliament, he decided to leave his position as an assistant to Mr. Cheam Channy and turn to a business to earn enough money to help continue his politics. Desiring, he decided to start a business and take time to do politics, when he started a company with friends to import cars for sale.
In the life of this former MP, according to Mr. Kang Kimhak, he likes politics, business and farming.
Mr. Kang Kimhak graduated from Sunthor Mok High School in 1999 and graduated with a Bachelor of Laws in 2011 from Norton University.
Mr. Kang Kimhak was born in Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province. He has eight siblings and is the sixth child in a family whose parents are farmers.
The 38-year-old married in 2007 and has four children, three boys and a girl, who are currently in charge.
Mr. Kang Kimhak: I miss and imagine that one day I will have the opportunity to sit in the National Assembly
Aspiration, combined with perseverance, will sometimes be as successful as desired, but how long that success stays with the aspirant can not be determined.
After all, Kang Kimhak met with success in life as his dream, which he dreamed of becoming an MP since he was young and achieved his goal, but the reality that happened to him Not stable for a desired period.
Indeed, former lawmaker Kang Kim Hak, before being elected to the National Assembly, he used to dream of doing politics to become an MP.
His dream soon became a reality, leading him to become a Member of Parliament for Kampong Cham province in the 2013 election in the fifth term.
But this success has been with him for more than two years, meaning he has been sitting in the National Assembly for about half of his five-year term.
While dreaming of becoming a member of parliament more than 10 years ago, Kang Kimhak used to be an assistant to former lawmaker Cheam Channy.
At the time, he was under the roof of the opposition Sam Rainsy Party, but because of his ambition to sit in the National Assembly, he left his job as an assistant and became a member of another opposition political party, Kem's Human Rights Party. Sokha.
After leaving Mr. Cheam Channy on the roof of the Sam Rainsy Party together, Mr. Kim Hak connected to continue politics with former lawmaker Mao Monivann in 2011.
