After the CNRP was formed, he was transferred by the leadership to help the Kampong Cham provincial party working group, standing as the 10th candidate for the National Assembly and being elected to the National Assembly in Kampong Cham in 2013.
I will never forget the time when HE Cheam Channy asked me to walk from room to room to the Assembly Hall, which was being prepared because the Assembly was being decorated in the Assembly Hall.
Later, I had an idea that I would go into business to earn money and have the resources to do political activities and become a politician.
Despite the unfavorable political situation, the former lawmaker has vowed not to withdraw from the political arena.
In the event that the political situation returns to normal, he will resume his political life, with strong hopes that the former CNRP will win the election to lead the country if the political environment is good and the election process is fair and inclusive. That CNRP.
Returning to the current political situation, 55 former lawmakers and 118 other senior CNRP officials were banned from politics for five years after their party was dissolved nearly four months ago. In Cambodia, even the media has a hard time communicating with them for interviews.
But on February 26, former lawmaker Kang Kimhak gave an interview to the Post expressing expectations for the former CNRP's return to run in this July's election. With its opponent of the same weight is the Cambodian People's Party, the ruling party of Prime Minister Hun Sen.
