In addition, Cambodians and Cambodians can also talk to each other to find a common solution for the national interest.
According to Kang Kimhak, after the CNRP was dissolved and more than 100 senior officials were stripped of their political rights, both party leaders and local members were concerned for their safety. Both intimidation and traction.
This concern is due to the fact that most of the leaders, as well as activists and members of the CNRP, refuse to surrender to the comfort or lure of ruling party officials.
That is why national leaders, as well as local leaders, decide to flee abroad or flee their villages to avoid threats.
