Ms. Kang Boran: On behalf of the royal family, I still have a notion of support, there is a video
Both the name and the appearance of the character are really beautiful as a Cambodian woman, and what this woman politician tried to endure, overcome all the difficulties from her past as a farmer to this point of success, should not be overlooked in this effort. Also.
Having been a politician since she was a young woman, Kang Boran has linked her life to the royalist FUNCINPEC political party under the leadership of Norodom Ranariddh since she was in her early 20s, expecting to reach her goal. And contribute to the service of society at any time.
With 20 years of patience, perseverance and perseverance, she gradually reached her goals, such as being a civil servant at the Ministry of Tourism, a former Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Tourism, and also a government adviser before becoming Phnom Penh Constituency Representative at present.
For a while, despite criticism of Norodom Ranariddh's FUNCINPEC royalist party, which had agreed to accept a split of the former CNRP's dissolved parliamentary seats, the party's leadership did not appear to be. Not interested in criticism.
The main focus for this party is to work with the ruling party, which is considered to serve the nation together for better peace and political stability for the development process.
Indeed, having a role in the public service of the state or as a servant in a state institution is considered a national service.
But for politicians and politicians who are not happy with this strategic national service, they do not support this kind of work.
They consider any political party that volunteers to work with the Cambodian People's Party, the ruling party of Prime Minister Hun Sen, to be just a puppet of the ruling party.
However, FUNCINPEC leaders have denied the allegations, calling them "painted" or "personal" and that FUNCINPEC is still a party with support and the Royalist Party remains united. Condolences to the people.
In an interview with the Post on February 19, Ms. Kang Boran, FUNCINPEC's only female MP, said:
With faith in the people's support, Ms. Kang Boran recalled the work of FUNCINPEC in the past, which brought peace, freedom, democracy and monarchy to Cambodia.
At the same time, for the work she is facing today, she said that since coming to the National Assembly as a member of parliament a few months ago, she, like other FUNCINPEC MPs, has been to the base to meet with the people many times.
Ms. Kang Boran added:
Roll up your sleeves and take off your pants to help solve and coordinate with the people who own the vote.
That is why each constituency is waiting to welcome all the MPs of the FUNCINPEC royal family.
Despite criticism that FUNCINPEC MPs are not the choice of the people in each locality or constituency, according to Ms. Kang Boran, in visiting each constituency, FUNCINPEC still has a reputation and remains a force. Active in fulfilling its role to bring peace to Cambodia.
Because what the royal family did on this occasion was the sole purpose of wanting the whole Cambodian society to be peaceful and politically stable.
However, this royal family still adheres to the position of maintaining the conditions for the Cambodian people to live in harmony with their homeland.
Dressed in traditional Khmer clothing to match her name with a fresh complexion that reflects the character of a real Khmer woman, Ms. Kang Boran, who has become a female MP in FUNCINPEC, said that her temperament is still not Far from the political arena.
Due to her political will, Kang Boran entered politics in 1997 in the ranks of the party's youth movement and in 2001-2008 as a member of the party's working group in Kandal province, and in 2008 she also came. Become a member of the Phnom Penh Capital Working Group.
Subsequently, from 2014 to the present, Ms. Kang Boran was also willing to be appointed by Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Ranariddh as his personal assistant and protocol.
She is also a member of the Board of Directors and a member of the Standing Committee of FUNCINPEC, which serves as the party's Deputy Secretary General.
For a vision for the future, she recommended strengthening the dissemination of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination against Women, including national laws, policies, regulations and measures that promote moral equality for women. Also, to ensure the participation of women by providing opportunities, status, role or in the field of decision-making to a high level.
However, in my recommendation, I would like to ask for the participation of women in empowerment by giving them positions in the field of employment as well as family society to make high decisions.
Increase national and international cooperation to increase the capacity of women in the public and political spheres.
Returning to his youth, Kang Boran was a student at Chaktomuk Secondary School and Preah Sisowath High School in Phnom Penh and graduated from Bakdup High School in 1997.
She graduated with a Bachelor's Degree in Management and Tourism in 2002 and further studied hospitality in Thailand, the Philippines and Singapore. In 2004, she completed a Master's Degree in Management and Tourism.
The woman politician was also a senior government official before becoming a Member of Parliament, which in 2003 Kang Boran was Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Tourism.
From 2014 to 2017, she was an advisor to the Royal Government and also a lecturer at various colleges.
Kang Boran is the bride of Kampong Cham and the second of two sisters in a family whose parents are farmers and teachers.
At the age of 41, Kang Boran is the loving and warm mother of two daughters in the family after their marriage in 2002.
In my career as a lawyer, I put justice first.
Choung Chou Ngy's lawyer: I believe that when the Cambodian justice system guarantees me, it will not be difficult to win the case
One word is said to have the nature to meet or have the same ideas to work together.
However, according to the interpretation of the above, it shows the same temperament and views, which is why lawyer Chou Chou Ngy Mean Veasna came to be a defense lawyer for the leaders and activists of the opposition.
From my point of view and my attitude, it is in line with the society, as in the case of Mr. Kim Sok, so Kim Sok is a social commentator, and he dares to speak and my temperament dares to criticize.
A prosperous society is also accompanied by criticism, but not all criticisms can be considered good lessons or ideas that the other party can accept, especially for the leaders of some countries or institutions. Satisfied with the criticism, even in a constructive sense.
Some leaders view critics as their backbone, and sometimes they can face legal action if they are too direct.
According to lawyer Choung Chou-Ngy, these factors are also an important part of motivating him to stand up for the person who is a vocal critic, as he understands that those critics really need legal services in case They suffer a lawsuit in any case.
Funds raised to serve that activity.
That action is a great idea that I have to do, so I can do it only once.
But for the lawyer he thinks is primarily useful, those actions are detrimental to economic interests.
Thus, if a lawyer is primarily interested, he does not come because it destroys his economy.
The sensitive political case, which began with Choung Chou-Ngy's lawyer, was the case of the removal of a Cambodian-Vietnamese border post in Svay Rieng province in 2010.
At the time, Sam Rainsy, the former president of the opposition Sam Rainsy Party, a client, removed a border post in Svay Rieng province's Chantrea district, which was seen by residents and politicians as being planted on Cambodian farmers' farmland.
Since then, the lawyer, who has never won a case, has continued to handle major opposition political cases until two opposition parties, the Sam Rainsy Party and Kem Sokha's Human Rights Party, merged into a major opposition party. The CNRP was dissolved in 2012 last year as the party gained momentum, with 55 lawmakers, 489 commune chiefs and more than 5,000 commune councilors.
The CNRP has always had a series of legal issues complained about by officials or leaders of the ruling Cambodian People's Party, Prime Minister Hun Sen, and his lawyer Choung Chou-Ngy and his colleagues have always appeared on the streets. The law is against the ruling party, but in all cases it never wins.
The lawyer stated:
Because at a very challenging stage, I put in a lot of effort, so when the justice system has a high percentage of guarantees of justice, I am able to win a case without difficulty.
However, as a seeker of justice, lawyer Chou Chou Ngy sees the word justice in Cambodia as the most difficult place to find because of the justice he seeks for the public today. One is very limited for Cambodian society.
But as a lawyer, Chou Chou Ngy has vowed not to give up the fight for justice, no matter what the circumstances. Strive to reduce the injustice that occurs as little as possible.
I am a citizen and a lawyer. If I give up, it means I have not fulfilled my role.
At the same time, he also criticized some lawyers who see the benefits mainly when they are working in the field of justice, which makes it impossible for them to work well in the field of justice.
But for Choung Chou-Ngy, the lawyer has made it clear that if he sees the main benefit, he will not be a lawyer, he will turn to running an investment company to make a profit.
Responding to an unscrupulous stance on money, the lawyer also expressed his pride as a lawyer who struggled for nothing.
Although he did not invest his career in law as a major interest, according to Chou Ngy, he did not face the problem of losing income through his career as a lawyer.
However, he can earn money to support his daily life without difficulty.
According to Ngy, there are two factors that make the justice system not good because of the ability and willingness of the organizers and managers in the field of justice.
If the administrators or organizers of the justice sector are capable but they are not willing to serve the sector, then the justice system is still narrow.
On the other hand, if the rulers are willing but incompetent, they will not be able to improve the justice system.
But it has to be divided into state plans. The government's plans are guaranteed. If the government does not have a clear plan, the people are the beneficiaries.
Therefore, the main guarantor of justice is the government through the Ministry of Justice.
Mr. Chou Ngy confirmed that:
Thus, the result is from the people voting until the government is elected, the government is responsible for justice.
So what level of justice results come from the government?
That is the responsibility of the government.
With regard to the limited justice system for Cambodian society today, he noted that this negative point is also due to the unwillingness or reluctance of most Cambodian jurists that they fear losing. Personal happiness.
They see greater benefits than social justice, and true justice is still far from being hungry for justice.
If the bar, the president of the bar must be a role model, if the court, the president of the bar must be a model.
If the minister is a role model, if the government, the prime minister is a role model.
After modeling and choosing the good people next to you to ensure responsibility.
Because those role models did not play a good role, our justice is limited.
In non-political, non-political cases protected by powerful individuals, Choung Chou-Ngy urged lawyers who have the discretion to make decisions to be willing to take risks and use their role as law enforcement effectively and responsibly. Deciding on the basis of the law to provide real justice to any party who is a victim in the case.
Otherwise, such a person is not qualified to be a judge.
I want responsible judges to dare to face Ahnong, and if they are under pressure, how can they not dare to defend justice?
Thus, he should resign.
Like me, if I do not dare to face, what can I do about the case involving the top leader of the opposition party?
Turning to Choung Chou-Ngy's academic and work seniority Before becoming an opposition lawyer, Ngy was a physics student at the Royal University of Phnom Penh in 1991 and became a professor of physics and taught the subject. Two years in 1996.
Satisfied with his work in the field of justice, Chou Ngy resigned as a teacher and returned to the law, graduating in 1995 with a bachelor's degree in law and a master's degree in law. 2008-2011.
Choung Chou-Ngy, originally from Preah Prosop commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province, is a former student of Hun Sen Khsach Kandal High School who graduated from high school in 1988.
He is the youngest of nine siblings in a family whose parents are farmers and of Chinese descent.
He said that we are human beings to know right from wrong, do not abuse them, love justice, protect justice.
This idea is a priceless legacy for me.
He has been married for five years, but the love affair has yet to provide a drop of blood for the couple's family.
10-year-old opposition lawyer never knows victory
Although Chung Chou-Ngy's lawyer, who has failed in this sensitive case, has not been discouraged from his role as a seeker of justice for the public, although he has never tasted success in political trials at the tribunal.
In all cases where he tried to legally defend his client in politics and still lost, Chou Chou Ngy's lawyer considered the failure to be just a form, but a success for the spirit of the effort.
