She graduated from high school or bankruptcy in 1974 in the Republic.
During the Second Kingdom of Cambodia, although she did not graduate from college, she completed many other courses on various subjects as well as human rights.
Mr. Yong Chan Sophear: Cambodia is ready to be the Vice President of the UN General Assembly
Despite some disagreements over respect for human rights and the recent UN Human Rights Council's rating on respect for human rights, Cambodia has not been documented. Not a bad list for the implementation of respect for human rights at the UN Human Rights Council, while Cambodia will also prepare to serve as Vice President of the United Nations General Assembly in 2019.
This was confirmed by Mr. Yong Chan Sophear, Ambassador, Deputy Permanent Representative of the Permanent Mission of Cambodia to the United Nations.
However, according to Mr. Yong Sophea, Cambodia, which has diplomatic relations with 193 countries, there are a few obstacles that are common in this field of diplomacy, but because the top leaders in the field of diplomacy, especially Foreign Minister Prak Sokhon is good at A balance between countries with which diplomatic relations have prevailed has pushed for a smooth diplomatic process, meaning that Cambodia is not biased towards any country.
Cambodia must have equal diplomatic relations and mutual respect with friendly countries, especially the five great powers.
Mr. Sophear said:
So the role is very big is that the ambassador in charge of this work must have a very strong position.
In an interview with the Post on December 9, the Ambassador Deputy Permanent Representative to the United Nations Mr. Yong Chan Sophear, who completed two diplomatic missions recently, saw a lot of progress in the field of Cambodian diplomacy on the international stage.
He said that from 1979 to 1991, when the Khmer Rouge was also holding a seat at the United Nations, the country seemed to be in isolation.
But after the 1993 national elections, Cambodia was no longer an isolated country, which meant that the country that had suffered under the Khmer Rouge regime began to have a new face and was recognized by the world to this day with equal honor. Equal face on the international stage under the leadership of Prime Minister Hun Sen.
With knowledge and experience working as a diplomat at the UN Yong Chan Sophear is trusted by government leaders and has been appointed director of the United Nations Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation for more than four months after completing his diplomatic mission at the United Nations. The second term is from 2005-2008, which is the first term of three years that he completed and returned to work in the country.
Until 2014-2017, the second mandate, he was appointed by the King as Deputy Permanent Ambassador at the Permanent Mission of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the United Nations in New York.
As a leader in the field of diplomacy, Mr. Sophear spoke about the roles and theories he has fulfilled in the past, both domestically and internationally, which shows that he is competent enough to fulfill his role as well as share. Share experience to civil servants and staff in the unit.
Before becoming a diplomat at the UN He also served as Deputy Director of the ASEAN Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation in 2009-2014.
Mr. Yong Chan Sophear graduated with a Master's Degree in International Relations Law from Washington, DC, USA in 2002.
In addition to studying abroad, he also completed a bachelor's degree in English and law in the country in 2000.
Apart from working as a civil servant, he is also a professor of the United Nations, teaching a second year bachelor's degree at the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
The main reason that motivates him to take the time to train students is to share knowledge with the next generation, which is his intention from childhood and also a link from the father who is a teacher.
Professor Yong Chan Sophear is also the author of a book entitled What Do They Do at the United Nations?
He wrote this book in order to contribute to raising the knowledge of Cambodian children to grow better.
Of course, this book can not satisfy all readers, but he hopes that this book will raise awareness for readers, scholars, researchers and those interested in understanding diplomacy, especially on the topic of organization. This peak is located at a distance of nearly 150,000 kilometers from Phnom Penh.
This book is a broad vision leading to world politics, in addition to talking about the United Nations, it also describes the contest for the Cambodian seat at the United Nations and the case of the Temple of Preah Vihear and even about borrowing maps. From the United Nations to verify in Phnom Penh.
In the future, they will not take this pool anymore, they will take all the educated people because they see that there is a lot of competition.
So, if we are still idle, we can not compete with them.
At the age of 43, Yong Chan Sophear has been with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for more than 20 years.
According to Mr. Sophear, the work that he has been doing every day is not with the help of any relatives, that is, his hard work and knowledge have driven him to the point of success in service. Nation through fair giving from the leadership.
Sophear is the third of five children in a family of civil servants and was originally from Phnom Penh, although his father was from Kampot and his mother was from Kampong Cham.
Mr. Sophear is a former student at Bak Touk High School and is married with two dependent children.
