Prisoners who talk on the wall are more likely to focus on eavesdropping, as the cell phone on the wall is designed to make it easier for inmates to speak, but not to speak fluently.
According to Mr. Sochua, the additional punishment for using a prison cell or disciplinary room to detain a prisoner for two levels is because the inmate uses a cell phone, uses drugs, and fights.
Anyone who violates prison rules will be placed in the cell, where cell phone use cases are held for two weeks, while in other cases Sochua is unsure how many days he will be held in the two-story jail. No.
