This is a positive point in prison.
But when asked if after more than two years in prison could discourage him from continuing his political career, Sochua seemed reluctant to answer.
It is an experience that we have been in prison for, and we talk about being careful and weighing things before we talk about actions.
So this is a lesson that every politician must learn.
The 59-year-old former French political prisoner has yet to return to politics after resigning as a senator from the Sam Rainsy Party and a member of the opposition party's executive committee. The CNRP, also a major opposition party, is another option he is facing.
Hong Sochua was pardoned by King Norodom Sihamoni on October 25 at the request of Prime Minister Hun Sen after he wrote a letter of condolence to Hun Sen acknowledging his actions. Correct to Hun Sen's leadership policy regarding the issue of the Cambodia-Vietnam border post.
Some politicians focus on international political pressure due to strong international pressure that prompted Hun Sen to release Hong Sochua.
Some see the release as a sign of Hun Sen's surrender to the CPP, but ruling party officials have dismissed such claims in response to a royal pardon at the request of the king. Mr. Hun Sen, because Mr. Hong Sochua acknowledged his mistakes and made Mr. Hun Sen sympathetic, decided to ask the King to pardon Mr. Sochua.
But Mr. Hong Sochua confirmed that:
Hong Sochua was arrested and jailed on August 15, 2015, on charges of falsifying public documents and using fake public documents in connection with posting on social media sensitive issues on the Cambodia-Vietnam border.
Mr. Sochua left Cambodia to live in France in January 1979 and studied for a Master's degree in Information Technology at the French Stock Exchange.
According to Hong Sochua, he has high blood pressure and will be leaving for France soon after his release from a doctor's appointment.
Turning to the dissolution of the CNRP by the ruling party Although the law has been signed by the King, but for Hong Sochua is optimistic that this large opposition party will not be able to Dissolved because it did not benefit Hun Sen's ruling party.
