ACLEDA is Cambodia's leading bank in terms of large and fast lending services, the largest number of employees, the largest number of branches and the first local bank to invest abroad, especially in Laos and Myanmar.
ACLEDA started the Small and Medium Business Plan Training Association for Cambodians and providing micro-loans in 1993 and became a bank in 2000.
The bank started a small association with a capital of more than 600,000 US dollars under the initiative of Mr. Channy and his colleagues.
Mr. In Channy recalled that after returning home in 1992, he worked for the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) and the International Labor Organization (ILO) for job creation and vocational training for small enterprises.
He has been put in charge of the Phnom Penh Economic Development Agency.
He said that at the time, ACLEDA received a $ 613,000 grant from the French Development Bank through UNDP.
At that time, a question arose as to who was responsible for recovering the debt after providing the loan?
Mr. Channy said that all of them, along with other colleagues, came together to find answers by studying the establishment process of various organizations, but at that time no organization provided pure credit, only programs related to illiteracy. Health.
It was not easy to mobilize the general population to come to the association's headquarters for training in small and medium-sized businesses in the early 1990s.
In 1993, the association produced a billboard describing the benefits of starting a business.
As a result, many traders come to study.
After listening to the business people who came to study, they realized that they came to study in order to borrow money from the association to run a small business to continue their ancestral business.
Mr. Channy said that in the first phase, for small businesses, the association did not require a house or land title in the event that they agreed to have at least five members in the same village.
Subsequently, they may be able to access loans with collateral.
The first program is to introduce savings.
He said that with a budget of more than 600,000 US dollars, members of the group, including him, feared that, as the old saying goes, chickens in the barn never eat rice for fear of being accused of embezzling the association's money. To avoid accusations, co-workers also suggest that the client be assessed as being able to repay on time.
To do so, ACLEDA staff and management have decided to establish an internal rule that all financial lending agents must not consume clients' fruits or juices.
Do this to avoid requesting a deferral from the customer.
It is the first internal law set forth by ACLEDA staff and management.
Whoever violates this order, the leadership has the right to stop without protest.
This is one of the secrets that enables ACLEDA to raise funds and increase customer trust.
I am clear with colleagues, colleagues listen to me and the whole organization has to listen to the majority of customers.
Regarding the decision to choose the swan as the symbol of ACLEDA Bank in 1993, he explained that at that time he came up with a temporary idea that if he decided to take the symbolic pig, he wanted his colleagues to join in finding any animal that They could not be humiliated, so all the members came up with a kind of animal king, the swan as a symbol of ACLEDA Bank.
He explained that the nature of the swan is the king of animals that like to land in a place with a clean environment, animals that like the cold, start with the letter H, the same as the word finance, and an animal that can save human life, which is worthy of the vision. And the mission of this bank.
After using the swan logo for 24 years, ACLEDA Bank was asked by the head of the Royal Government, Prime Minister Hun Sen, to change the swan logo for fear that people would mistake it for a state-owned bank.
This swan logo is also used by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
ACLEDA Bank spent $ 3.5 million to replace the logo in more than a week.
Another secret that led to ACLEDA Bank's rapid and successful expansion of branches from the municipal, provincial, district and commune levels is modern technology, in which Cambodia has a fiber optic network and a smart phone system.
These ideas came with the participation of bank staff.
