Mr. In Channy has a life story similar to that of ordinary Cambodians in Cambodia, going through the Khmer Rouge communist regime.
His family was evacuated from Phnom Penh to Prey Veng province, his parents' hometown in Sithor Kandal district.
The Khmer Rouge did not allow the family there, so they evacuated again to Battambang province near the Thai border.
In 1979, when Vietnam exiled the Khmer Rouge, he continued to live in Battambang until 1981, when he went to study and live in a camp near the Thai border.
In Channy, now 56, was married in 1996 and has four children, two daughters and two sons.
