Mick Lian: Economic slowdown due to lack of ideas
After all, a country, a nation, it can move forward or backward, depends entirely on the right thinking, right analysis and right decisions of the leaders and citizens of that country.
This is what 63-year-old Dr. Mik Lian, who is currently a senior adviser to the Supreme National Economic Council (SNEC), said.
Kalyan has spent more than half of his life living, visiting, studying and working in more than 100 countries around the world.
Last week, Dr. Mey Kalyan spent more than two hours sharing his knowledge, skills and personal experiences with the Post, starting with his vision, mission, work history and experience after receiving a scholarship to study at Japan received a doctorate in economics in 1974, a year before the Khmer Rouge took power.
The Khmer Rouge seizes power from the regime of General Lon Nol on April 17, 1975.
