He said he saw that the reason why the Cambodian economy was slowing down compared to other countries in the region was that human resources were still limited, and that there was a lack of ideas to think, research and build long-term strategies.
Thinking is not imaginary, but must have a clear purpose, do or not on a clear analysis.
That is the most important thing for our country.
So until we look at the history of our country.
If we want the country to be more advanced, Cambodians need to know where we are strong.
And where is the weakness?
Mr. Mey Kalyan said:
If we compare with the countries in ASEAN, our per capita income has almost dropped to 9 or 10.
Clearly, we are a little more advanced, a little easier, but we are still poor.
