On the other hand, he has the opportunity to ask and interview people in general, politicians, leaders, not only in Cambodia, that is, only those who do something can have a positive impact on others or society. Or negative.
When the Khmer Rouge came to power at the age of seven, Puy Kea's family was evacuated from Phnom Penh near Phnom Chheu Kach in Prey Veng province's Ba Phnom district, and his father died there in 1978. Last year, the Pol Pot regime was overthrown.
As a child and teenager living along the Mekong River near the Neak Leung crossing, Puy Kea went on as a child selling cakes on a ferry, selling fried bananas and running a noodle table to earn money to support his family. Owned by a widowed mother.
Puy Kea became an outstanding student of literature in Kandal province in 1985 and then went on to study at Chaktomuk School in Phnom Penh before attending Sisowath High School in 1987, then called the school. Phnom Daun Penh, with the help of a foster brother who works as a teacher in Phnom Penh.
After starting my career as a journalist in 1994, I went on to study journalism in Thailand, the Philippines, Japan, Germany and the United States.
