Mr. Chhun recalled that on October 10, 2005, government leaders traveled to Hanoi to sign a supplementary agreement to the 1985 territorial integrity agreement with Vietnam.
As a member of the Cambodian Watchdog Council, Chhun sees the 1985 treaty as a loss of Cambodian territory because it was a bilateral treaty signed in the 1980s while Cambodia was under control. Vietnam's seal, and this treaty has already been ratified by the Paris Peace Accords of October 23, 1991.
On October 15, 2005, Chhun was jailed by the government for his outspoken criticism of the ever-sensitive Cambodia-Vietnam border issue.
